What is ECR?

 ECR is a fully managed Docker container registry by AWS — it allows you to store, manage, and deploy container images securely and at scale.

🔥 Key Features:

🔒 Secure image storage with AWS IAM & encryption
🤖 CI/CD integration with CodeBuild, CodePipeline, Jenkins
🧠 Vulnerability scanning for image security
🧹 Lifecycle policies to clean up old images
⚡ Seamless integration with ECS & EKS

💬 Real-world Use Case:

 In my projects, I use ECR to store Docker images built in CodeBuild and automatically deploy them via CodePipeline to ECS. It keeps the deployment flow clean, versioned, and fully automated.

💡 Pro Tip:

 Always tag your images (e.g., v1, latest, build-number) — it helps track versions easily during rollbacks and deployments.
